1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,350
This is cheeseOS:

2
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:04,160
the health twin that keeps working

3
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:05,900
when Earth goes quiet.

4
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:09,460
First, say or type how you feel.

5
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:10,720
Your speech is transcribed

6
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,950
right on the device,

7
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:14,040
in English or Portuguese.

8
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,530
Your 3D twin lights up.

9
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:17,690
Each symptom is mapped

10
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:19,440
to one of seven body regions,

11
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:21,660
and coloured by how severe it is.

12
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:26,030
Then you get clear next steps,

13
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:27,290
with no connection.

14
00:00:27,310 --> 00:00:29,370
It all runs on local rules.

15
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:32,260
AI is optional, never required.

16
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:35,920
Your vital signs are compared

17
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,380
against reference ranges

18
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,950
from NASA and NIH sources.

19
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:40,640
In this demo,

20
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,950
the readings are simulated.

21
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,840
Red flags always come first.

22
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:47,600
Chest pain with shortness of breath

23
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,120
turns the screen critical,

24
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:51,580
and shows what to do right now.

25
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:54,000
And there's more.

26
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:56,000
Training: the camera counts

27
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:57,990
your repetitions, on the device.

28
00:00:58,010 --> 00:00:59,900
A full log and report,

29
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:01,790
ready for the flight surgeon.

30
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:03,400
And the mission science:

31
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:06,440
NASA's five hazards, with sources.

32
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:08,670
cheeseOS.

33
00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:11,600
Health that travels as far as we do.
